David I asked this question in another post, but I'll repeat here.
Since you don't play the protection racket that means you get divine
protection later. What I want to know is what do you do to manage AC
in the meantime and how do you manage the negative effects?

AC has three primary sources:

1) Armor
2) Magical
3) Divine

Eventually all three are available to the average character and the point
is moot. But in the early game options are somewhat limited. enchant armor
is unknown, and holy water is unavailable generally.

So of the three armor is easiest to get in the early game. But it has two
negative effects:

1) weight
2) spellcasting impact

Now the effect of those two depends on the character class. Combat wombats
have good strength and con and poor spellcasting ability. OTOH spellcasters
have the opposite. So the wearing of armor impacts them in vastly different
ways.

Note that magical and divine AC have neither of these negative effects.

I'm sure I'm attached to the protection run because I generally run
spellcasters. I feel the effects of wearing armor. I become burdened. I
can cast spells with it on. It's a high priority to ditch armor yet have
a usable AC going into mid game. The protection racket provides that as a
route. It's the only reliable way to get divine protection in the early game.

Note I don't run the classic protection racket. I work hard to up my HP and
lower my AC will executing the run. Most times I hit mine town at XL2 or XL3
with between 25-30 HP with the XL9 72HP pet. 

But if you don't run it, then how do you manage these issues, especially if
you're running a spellcaster class?

1) Run with a higher AC?
2) Wear armor with its negative effects?
3) Work diligently to get magical AC?
4) Level up with a combo of 1-3 above then purchase protection?
5) Heavily rely on pets as a HP buffer?
6) Something else I haven't thought of?

Generally during the run I do #2. I have the pet curse test every item I
come across and where anything that's uncursed. So dwarven mithril, or
banded, or plate are all options during the run. I'll simply operate burdened
without the ability to case spells until I get divine protection.

If you get a chance can you outline a thought process. Maybe I'll learn 
something new I can try.

